# Everything outside the preview site. outputDirectory already limits what is
# served; this keeps it out of the upload as well.
proposals/
libraries/
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
.remember/

# Build and test machinery. Verified as referenced by no page: the only link
# into a non-asset directory is design-system/tests/motion-contracts.html, which
# is kept.
design-system/tools/
design-system/src/
design-system/package.json
design-system/package-lock.json

# The library's manifest and its README. `design-system/core/` itself is served
# — the site loads the resolver, the theme, the icons and the fonts from it —
# but the package's own metadata is not part of the site.
design-system/core/package.json
design-system/core/README.md

# Verification evidence that no served page links to. The report links to the
# capture READMEs, which are kept; the reference baselines and the approved image
# sets are for reviewing this repository, not for publishing. Roughly 10MB of a
# 23MB upload, and none of it is reachable from the site.
design-system/validation/baselines/
design-system/reference/material-examples/
design-system/reference/approved-crystal/
design-system/reference/approved-controls/

# The preserved source archive. These are immutable copies of the design Crystal
# was built out from, kept with SHA-256 digests as an internal provenance record.
# They are not published: the site describes Crystal as Meridian Digital's own
# system, and the archive names its origin. Kept in the repository, where the
# record belongs, rather than rewritten — a provenance record that has been
# edited is not a provenance record.
design-system/reference/gather-approved-baseline.md
design-system/reference/gather-crystal-recipes.json
design-system/reference/gather-materials.md
design-system/reference/provenance.json

# Never publishable.
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
design-system/crystal-design-system.zip
